\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O For a thousand tongues to sing 
\par My great Redeemer's praise,
\par The glories of my God and King,
\par The triumphs of His grace !
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. My gracious Master and my God,
\par Assist me to proclaim, 
\par To spread through all the earth abroad
\par The Honours of thy name
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Jesus! the name that charms our Fears, 
\par That bids our sorrows cease;
\par "Tis music in the sinner's ears,
\par 'Tis life, and health, and peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. He speaks, and, listening to His voices,
\par  New life the dead receive,
\par The mournful, broken hearts rejoice,
\par The humble poor believe.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. He breaks the power of cancelled sin,
\par He sets the prisoner free;
\par His blood can make the foulest clean,
\par His blood availed for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. See all your sins on Jesus laid:
\par The Lamb of God was slain,
\par His soul was once an offering made
\par For every soul of man.
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

